# Deployment constants, shared by both deploy paths.
#
# The client id used to live in two places — typed into deploy.sh by hand, and
# stored as a GitHub Actions variable. Nothing kept them in agreement, so every
# Actions deploy silently overwrote whatever the last manual deploy had set, and
# sign-in broke again with no obvious connection to the commit that did it.
#
# It lives here now because it is not a secret: a Google client id names the app
# to Google and grants nothing on its own. It is served to every visitor's
# browser by design. Both paths read this file; an environment variable of the
# same name still overrides it, for testing against a second client.
#
# ALLOWED_EMAILS is deliberately NOT here — who may write is per-person config,
# and it stays a GitHub Actions variable / an argument to deploy.sh.

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=845964113753-ie5eec2bohmi7bkroand5oljgsc0bq2m.apps.googleusercontent.com
